# Netlify headers, applied only when `astro/dist` is a site's publish
# directory -- that is, the standalone Astro preview site. Netlify
# reads `_headers` at the publish root only, so this file does nothing
# when the build is copied into a subdirectory of another site.
#
# Keeps every response out of search engines while the Astro build is
# not the published website. `robots.txt` alongside this file allows
# crawling on purpose, so that crawlers fetch each page and see this
# header.
#
# Remove at cutover, and never copy this file over the Jekyll site's
# `_headers` when merging output: that file carries the website's
# caching and security headers.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
